{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ממזר", :translit "mamzer", :gloss "mamzer"} {:he "ב' במסורה", :translit "bet b'masorah", :gloss "two times in the Masorah"} {:he "וישב ממזר באשדוד", :translit "v'yashav mamzer b'ashdod", :gloss "and a mamzer shall dwell in Ashdod"} {:he "עתידין ממזרים ליטהר ויתישבו בארץ", :translit "atidin mamzerim l'itaheir v'yityashvu b'aretz", :gloss "mamzerim are destined to be purified and settle in the land"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ממזר" "וישב ממזר באשדוד"]}], :frame {:text "The verse in Zechariah 9:6 — 'a mamzer shall dwell in Ashdod' — is read as a promise of future rehabilitation. The Sages debate the eschatological status of mamzerim: one view states that in the future God will purify them (Kiddushin 72b), while another holds they will not be purified but will be distinguishable (Yevamot 89a). The Ba'al HaTurim cites the tradition of future purification and links it to the word 'settle' (v'yityashvu) echoing Zechariah's language of 'dwell' (v'yashav).", :sources ["Zechariah 9:6" "Kiddushin 72b" "Yevamot 89a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא יבא ממזר בקהל ה'", :translit "lo yavo mamzer b'kahal Hashem", :gloss "a mamzer shall not enter the congregation of the Lord"} {:he "ממזר", :translit "mamzer", :gloss "mamzer"} {:he "פצוע דכה", :translit "patzua dakah", :gloss "crushed of testicles"} {:he "שממזר אינו מוליד כפצוע דכא", :translit "she'mamzer eino molied k'fatzua dakah", :gloss "for a mamzer does not beget like a crushed one"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah (juxtaposition): adjacent terms ממזר and פצוע דכה in Deut 23:2-3"}], :frame {:text "The Torah juxtaposes the prohibition of mamzerim with that of crushed or severed men in Deut 23:2–3. The principle of semikhat parshiyot, that the Torah's juxtapositions carry legal significance, is used here to infer that a mamzer shares with the crushed man the quality of not propagating his line. The legal definition of a mamzer is established in Mishnah Kiddushin 3:12, and the exclusion of both categories from the congregation is treated in Mishnah Yevamot 8:2.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 23:2-3" "Mishnah Kiddushin 3:12" "Mishnah Yevamot 8:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ממזר" "וישב ממזר באשדוד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ממזר", :refs ["Deuteronomy 23:3" "Zechariah 9:6"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וישב ממזר באשדוד", :refs ["Zechariah 9:6"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhah (juxtaposition): adjacent terms ממזר and פצוע דכה in Deut 23:2-3", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:35.164340085Z", :model "glm-5.2"}